======== A. atom at bit-identical equality, each relation (family contrast_j, threshold 0.25)
A GT strict: within=False truth=False agree=True  -> ok
A LT strict: within=False truth=False agree=True  -> ok
A NE strict: within=False truth=False agree=True  -> ok
A LE non-strict: within=False truth=True agree=True  -> ok
A GE non-strict: within=False truth=True agree=True  -> ok
======== B. the same with the threshold given on each side (l9_threshold == threshold), and the controls
B identical numbers and thresholds: within=False truth=False
B identical numbers, thresholds one ulp apart (inside the bar): within=True (undetermined kept)
B numbers one ulp apart against 0: within=True (undetermined kept)
B +0.0 vs -0.0 against 0: within=False truth=False (Python == decides a signed-zero pair)
B nan both sides: within=False truth=None agree=False (not known: never decided)
======== C. each producer relation at equality next to the comparator's encoding (x == threshold on both sides)
C ok       producer=True  comparator=True   equals_primary (sensitivity.py:303/320 _same; comparator NE on sensitivity - primary, word = not any)
