C summary: 15 relations, 0 mismatched at equality
======== D. the representation gap: _same is a canonical JSON digest (idle_admission.canonical_sha256)
D primary=0.0 sensitivity=-0.0: producer _same=False (equals_primary printed False); comparator relation(==)=True, atom within=False truth=False -> word decided True  <- producer False vs comparator True: DISAGREE (over-refusal) if ever printed
D primary=1 sensitivity=1.0: producer _same=False (equals_primary printed False); comparator relation(==)=True, atom within=False truth=False -> word decided True  <- producer False vs comparator True: DISAGREE (over-refusal) if ever printed
D note: a sensitivity value equal to its primary value in binary64 but differing in sign of zero or in JSON number representation is the only pair the two encodings classify differently; both sides' values are computed by the same code path under an equal bound (b_sens == b_op), so no producer path is shown to print one.
